  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/bore.rs`: the bore opts into the ring ladder's ramp (`Motion::with_ring_zig`, from #1609). A Bore with entry Ramp and no entry ramp angle now zig-zags along the radial sweep at the transition's ramp angle (`Links::ramp_angle`, 3 deg by default). Before, it took the chord from the last ring start to the centre. That chord is one ring radius long, so it descended at up to 84 deg at the cutting feed.\n- A sweep that is too short for the ramp (more than 64 legs) gets a plunge at the plunge feed with an `entry:` note. This is the existing `Descent::Sub` path.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/ladder_links.rs`: the pass link that lifts after the sweep and plunges back down the same column to start the ring now writes an `entry:` note when the entry is not Plunge. The moves do not change.\n- The decision is in `docs/decisions/1665-bore-ramp-angle.md`. No new parameter: the ramp angle is the existing transition ramp angle, the same one the Circular reads.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New suite `crates/motion/tests/bore_ramp_angle.rs`:\n  - `a_ramp_entry_bore_never_descends_steeper_than_its_ramp_angle`: the issue repro (Ø7) plus Ø12 and Ø16, climb and conventional. Every descending feed move is at most the ramp angle, or an axial move at the plunge feed with an `entry:` note.\n  - `the_ring_restart_plunge_of_a_ramp_entry_bore_is_named`: the ring restart plunge has an `entry:` note.\n- Both tests are red on `origin/main` 389fe96c (an axial descent at feed 500 with no note, and no restart note). Each test is red without its half of the fix.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on 16b4bf0b: green (motion lib, bore_ramp_angle, center_cut_law, circular_ramp_angle, corner_blend, entry_approach, level_links, predrilled_entry, refusal_ghost, tiny_step, xy_arc_entry; app bore_entry, ladder_entry_height). Also `motion:one_descent` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The app suites that build a bore through the document (`mill2d_c`, `operations`, app `level_links`) and the release heavy lanes. No golden changed in the suites that ran. No bore golden `.cl`/`.nc` exists.\n- The GUI was not started.\n\nChangelog: Bore with entry Ramp descends at the ramp angle along the radial sweep (or a named plunge), not on a steep chord at the cutting feed; the ring restart plunge is named.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1665\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
